@node Bytecode File Format
@subsection Bytecode File Format

The fcvm executes Franc C bytecode files.

They have the following header structure:

@example
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Magic Number (4 bytes)              │  0x45 0x0C 0x45 0x0C
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Bytecode Instructions               │  Variable length
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
@end example

@strong{Magic Number}: @samp{0x45 0x0C 0x45 0x0C} (4 bytes), as defined in the
@ref{Bytecode reference, , Franc C bytecode reference}. - Validates file
format at VM initialization - Invalid magic number triggers immediate
error

@node Command-Line Interface
@subsection Command-Line Interface

@example
./fcvm <bytecode_file>
@end example

