@node Memory Layout (1)
@subsection Memory Layout

The VM maintains three core structures:

@itemize
@item
The operand stack
@item
The callstack
@item
Three specific registers
@end itemize

@enumerate
@item
@anchor{Operand Stack}Operand Stack


Stores temporary computation values, variables and function return
values.

@example
┌─────────────┬─────────────┬─────────────┐
│  Element 0  │  Element 1  │  Element 2  │
│  (8 bytes)  │  (8 bytes)  │  (8 bytes)  │
└─────────────┴─────────────┴─────────────┘
      ↑
    Stack Top
@end example

@strong{Properties}: - Type: @samp{[Word8]} (list of bytes) - Element size: 8 bytes
(64-bit) - Initial state: One zero element @samp{[0x00 × 8]} - Max size:
1,000,000 elements (8 MB) - Operations: PUSH (prepend), POP (drop first
8 bytes)

@item
@anchor{Call Stack}Call Stack


Manages function call frames.

@example
┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│  Frame: (PC: 0, SP: 0)          │  ← Entry
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  Frame: (PC: 12, SP: 16)        │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  Frame: (PC: 57, SP: 24)        │  ← Current
└─────────────────────────────────┘
@end example

@strong{Properties}: - Type: @samp{[(PC, SP)]} (list of tuples) - Frame content:
Return address (PC) + Stack pointer (SP) - Initial state: Empty @samp{[]} -
Max depth: 1,000,000 frames

@strong{Behavior}: - @samp{CALL}: Push @samp{(PC+1, SP)}, jump to function - @samp{RET}: Pop
frame, restore context, trim stack - @strong{Termination}: Empty call stack
after @samp{RET} → program ends

@item
@anchor{Registers}Registers


@strong{Program Counter (PC)} - Points to current instruction in bytecode -
Initial: 8 (after 4-byte magic number) - Updates: @samp{+1} (normal), @samp{+9}
(with data), or jump target

@strong{Stack Pointer (SP)} - Marks base of current function's stack frame -
Used for local variable access via @samp{PUSHREL=/=POPREL} - Modified during
@samp{CALL} and @samp{RET}

@strong{Zero Flag (ZF)} - Type: @samp{Word8} (0 or 1) - Initial: 1 (true) -
Semantics: @samp{0} if stack top = 0, else @samp{1} - Set by @samp{ZFLAG}, tested by
@samp{ZJMP}
@end enumerate

