@node Function Call Convention
@subsection Function Call Convention

@strong{Calling sequence}:

@example
1. Push function address
2. Execute CALL
   → Saves (PC+1, SP) to call stack
   → Jumps to function
@end example

@strong{Return sequence}:

@example
1. Execute RET
   → Restores PC and SP
   → Trims stack to SP position
   → If call stack empty: program terminates
@end example

@strong{Stack frame layout}:

@example
┌──────────────────┐
│  Caller frame    │
├──────────────────┤  ← SP
│  Local function  │  ← Stack top
└──────────────────┘
@end example

@node Exceptions List
@section Exceptions List

All errors exit with code @strong{84} and write to @strong{stderr}.

@menu
* Load-Time Errors::
* Runtime Errors::
@end menu

@node Load-Time Errors
@subsection Load-Time Errors

@strong{Invalid Magic Number}

@example
Message: *** UNRECONIZED FILE FORMAT
Trigger: First 4 bytes ≠ 0x45 0x0C 0x45 0x0C
@end example

@strong{File I/O Error}

@example
Message: Error with file
Trigger: File not found, permission denied, or read error
@end example

@node Runtime Errors
@subsection Runtime Errors

@strong{Arithmetic Errors}

@example
Message: *** 0 CAN'T BE USE in this operation
Trigger: DIV or MOD with divisor = 0
@end example

@strong{Stack & CallStack Overflow}

@example
Message: *** STACK OVERFLOW
Trigger: Operand stack ≥ 1M elements OR call stack ≥ 1M frames
Cause:   Excessive PUSH without POP, or infinite recursion
@end example

@strong{Stack Underflow}

@example
Message: *** STACK ERROR
Trigger: Operation requires elements when stack_size ≤ 1
Affects: All binary/unary ops, CALL, JMP, ZJMP, AFF
@end example

@node Known Caveats
@section Known Caveats

@menu
* Undefined Behaviors::
* Performance Limitations::
* Portability Issues::
@end menu

@node Undefined Behaviors
@subsection Undefined Behaviors

@strong{Integer Overflow} - 64-bit signed integers wrap silently - Example:
@samp{INT64_MAX + 1} → UNDEFINED - No error raised

@strong{Invalid Opcodes} - Treated as NOP (PC += 1) - Corrupted bytecode may
execute partially - No detection mechanism

@node Performance Limitations
@subsection Performance Limitations

@strong{List-Based Stack} - Push/Pop: O(1) ✓ - SP-relative access: O(n) ✗ -
Impact: Slow for deep stacks (>1000 elements)

@strong{String Operations} - @samp{AFFS} creates intermediate structures - Linear in
string length (acceptable)

@node Portability Issues
@subsection Portability Issues

@strong{Platform Word Size} - @samp{PC} and @samp{SP} use Haskell @samp{Int} type - 32-bit
systems: Max ~2GB bytecode - 64-bit systems: Max ~8GB bytecode - Not a
practical concern for typical use

