@node Académie Franc C'Aise
@section Académie Franc C'Aise

@samp{Académie Franc C'Aise} is the @samp{functional tester} made in @samp{Python} for
the @samp{Franc C}, and uses @samp{Larousse} standard library.

You will find in every single @samp{Larousse} source code function: - The
same function written in @samp{C}. - A main function in @samp{Franc C} which calls
the function in @samp{Franc C} with various parameter, in the @samp{test}
folder. - A main function in @samp{C} which calls the function in @samp{C} with
the same parameters, in the @samp{test} folder.

@samp{Académie Franc C'Aise} compiles both the @samp{C} and @samp{Franc C} version
using @samp{gcc} and @samp{fcvm}. It then runs both versions, and check whether
their inputs are the same as a way to test the language. It also
displays how much time each step took (Compilation, Execution) for both
languages then finally shows the time difference between those.

@samp{Franc C} is in most cases faster to compile than @samp{C}. However, @samp{C} is
almost always faster in execution time than @samp{Franc C}.

At the end of the program, @samp{Académie Franc C'Aise} displays how many
tests passed out of how many were run. It then exits with a failure if
not all tests passed.

@bye
